issue(id="0020" status="review")
  title Publish dprint-plugin-pug as a Wasm npm package
  user-story
    as-a dprint user in an npm-managed JavaScript or web-tooling project
    i-want to install dprint-plugin-pug from npm and reference it with dprint's `npm:` plugin resolver
    so-that my package manager and lockfile can manage the Pug formatter plugin without downloading from a separate plugin host
  premise.
    The `dprint-plugin-pug` crate already builds to a single Wasm plugin, which
    is the distribution shape dprint recommends for sandboxed formatter
    plugins. Dprint now supports npm plugin specifiers, including pinned registry
    versions and unversioned `node_modules` lookups. This should be a much
    simpler package than the native `puggers` npm surface: stage
    `dprint_plugin_pug.wasm` as `plugin.wasm`, publish a small npm package, and
    wire it into the existing lockstep Knope and OIDC release flow.
  acceptance-criteria
    criterion Add an npm package for the dprint plugin, preferring the package name `dprint-plugin-pug` if it remains available when implementation starts.
    criterion Package the release Wasm artifact as `plugin.wasm` with a minimal `package.json`, README, and `getPath(): string` JavaScript/type entrypoint compatible with standard dprint Wasm plugin npm packages.
    criterion Add repeatable build and pack commands that compile `crates/dprint-plugin-pug` for `wasm32-unknown-unknown --release` and stage only the npm package files needed by dprint.
    criterion Verify the package works through dprint's npm resolver using both a pinned form such as `npm:dprint-plugin-pug@<version>` and a package-manager-managed local form such as `npm:dprint-plugin-pug`.
    criterion Keep the package version in lockstep with the Rust workspace and existing npm package family through Knope version files and version-alignment checks.
    criterion Integrate npm trusted publishing through GitHub Actions OIDC so release CI publishes the dprint plugin npm package alongside the existing package group.
    criterion Document installation and dprint configuration examples for npm users, including when to use pinned npm specifiers versus local `node_modules` resolution.
    criterion Add a Knope change file using `default` frontmatter that summarizes the new npm distribution path for the dprint plugin.
  review-items
    item(status="open") Claim `dprint-plugin-pug` on npm and configure the trusted publisher for `.github/workflows/release.yml` before the first release publish.
